{"version":"ai-mcq-bank-v2-la-batch15-high-quality-rewritten-affected-2026-05-22-stem-fixed-inequality-rendering-fixed-student-facing-qc-2026-05-31-pt-foundations-2026-06-11-pt-batch2-foundations-counting-2026-06-11-pt-batch3-counting-probability-rules-2026-06-11-pt-batch4-conditioning-2026-06-11-pt-batch5-random-variables-2026-06-11-pt-batch6-discrete-distributions-2026-06-11-pt-batch7-distribution-foundations-2026-06-11-pt-batch8-continuous-expectation-2026-06-11-pt-batch9-non-week7-expectation-transform-2026-06-11-pt-batch10-non-week7-process-summary-2026-06-11-pt-batch11-non-week7-final-summary-shape-2026-06-11-quality-round1-2026-06-14-quality-round2-2026-06-14-quality-round3-2026-06-14-quality-round4-deep-2026-06-14+quality-round5-difficulty-2026-06-14+quality-round6-expression-2026-06-14+quality-round7-answer-cue-2026-06-14+quality-round8-answer-shape-2026-06-14+quality-round9-answer-position-2026-06-14+quality-round10-template-padding-2026-06-14+quality-round11-generic-stems-2026-06-14+quality-round12-deterministic-cleanup-2026-06-15+quality-pilot-deep-rework-2026-06-15+v3-2026-10-04+upright-2026-10-04+v3-2026-10-04+v3-2026-10-06+v3-2026-10-06+qa-fixes-2026-10-08","concept_id":"Year-1/2b-Probability-Distributions/joint-probability-density-function.html","concept":{"concept_id":"Year-1/2b-Probability-Distributions/joint-probability-density-function.html","questions":[{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $(X,Y)$ have joint density $f_{X,Y}$, and let $B\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}^2$ be a region. Which formula computes $\\mathbb{P}((X,Y)\\in B)$ for every such pair and set?","options":["$f_{X,Y}(x,y)$ at one point $(x,y)$ of $B$","$\\iint_B f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y$","$\\iint_B f_X(x)f_Y(y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y$","$\\sum_{(x,y)\\in B}f_{X,Y}(x,y)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d5ddcc01a8425273050d6bc1","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which condition must a joint density satisfy?","options":["$0\\le f_{X,Y}\\le1$ everywhere","$\\int f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x=1$ for every $y$","$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=f_{X,Y}(y,x)$ for all $x,y$","$f_{X,Y}\\ge0$ with total integral $1$ over the plane"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2b6c715d8836ec2fefdb8175","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For a pair with a joint density, what is $\\mathbb{P}(X=Y)$?","options":["$0$","$\\tfrac12$, by symmetry","$\\int f_{X,Y}(x,x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","It depends on the density"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2561c699949a37d2d238f208","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A joint density is continuous at $(x,y)$ and satisfies $f_{X,Y}(x,y)=3$. For small positive $h$ and $k$, which expression approximates $\\mathbb{P}((X,Y)\\in[x,x+h]\\times[y,y+k])$?","options":["$3hk$","$hk$","$3(h+k)$","$9hk$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"81eb4eef47540b92f10444b3","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which joint density describes independent $X$ and $Y$?","options":["$8xy$ on $0<x<y<1$","$x+y$ for $0<x,y<1$","$4xy$ on $(0,1)^2$","$2$ on $0<x<y<1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"977418fec2e4cdd12b2779c6","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"A point $(X,Y)$ is chosen uniformly in the unit square. Find the probability that it lies below the parabola, $\\mathbb{P}(Y<X^2)$.","options":["$\\tfrac12$","$\\tfrac13$","$\\tfrac23$","$\\tfrac14$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4e3446c8173cff705ff995f1","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For which constant $c$ is $f(x,y)=c\\,xy^2$ on the unit square a joint density?","options":["$3$","$2$","$\\tfrac16$","$6$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bf3820fac12b5ad8eb8e48ba","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $(X,Y)$ have density $8xy$ on $0<y<x<1$. What is $\\mathbb{P}(X<\\tfrac12)$?","options":["$\\tfrac14$","$\\tfrac1{16}$","$\\tfrac12$","$\\tfrac18$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bd1a8600d1d38f8188df7952","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_009","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"The pair $(X,Y)$ has density $3x$ on $0<y<x<1$ and zero elsewhere. Compute $\\mathbb{P}(Y>\\tfrac12)$.","options":["$\\tfrac12$","$\\tfrac18$","$\\tfrac5{16}$","$\\tfrac34$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e153657b76aa6ebe1afb557e","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"$(X,Y)$ is uniform on the unit disc $x^2+y^2<1$. What is $\\mathbb{P}(X^2+Y^2<\\tfrac19)$?","options":["$\\tfrac13$","$\\tfrac89$","$\\tfrac\\pi9$","$\\tfrac19$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"67853740c7647299002734f1","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A joint density is changed to the value $100$ on the segment $\\{(x,\\tfrac12):0<x<1\\}$ and left unchanged elsewhere. What happens to probabilities?","options":["Every region meeting the segment gains probability","The total probability exceeds $1$","Nothing changes","Only probabilities of regions containing the whole segment change"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"90fa0edfb9664fd403e6d335","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"The pair $(X,Y)$ has joint density $f$ satisfying $f(x,y)=f(y,x)$ for all $x,y$. Which statement about $\\mathbb{P}(X<Y)$ follows?","options":["It depends on how much density lies near the diagonal","It equals $\\tfrac12$: equal mass on each side, none on the diagonal","It equals $\\tfrac12$ only if $X$ and $Y$ are independent","It is below $\\tfrac12$, since the diagonal carries some probability"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c78f12bd673d6883543be683","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A joint density $f$ is supported on $0<x<y<1$. Which iterated integral gives $\\mathbb{P}(Y<\\tfrac12)$?","options":["$\\int_{1/2}^1\\int_0^yf(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y$","$\\int_0^{1/2}\\int_y^1f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y$","$\\int_0^1\\int_0^{1/2}f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y$","$\\int_0^{1/2}\\int_0^yf(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9d405697dd82efd891b891df","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"The pair $(X,Y)$ has joint density $f(x,y)=x+y$ on $(0,1)^2$ and zero elsewhere. What is $\\mathbb{P}(Y>2X)$?","options":["$\\tfrac5{24}$","$\\tfrac14$","$\\tfrac{19}{24}$","$\\tfrac1{24}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2082c0ca93d13cb8980b7dfa","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"$X\\sim\\operatorname{Exp}(2)$ and $Y\\sim\\operatorname{Exp}(1)$ are independent, with rates $2$ and $1$. Integrating the joint density, what is $\\mathbb{P}(X>2Y)$?","options":["$\\tfrac13$","$\\tfrac45$","$\\tfrac15$","$\\tfrac12$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ce3ce7192c63b7789bda3a92","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $(X,Y)$ have density $4xy$ on $(0,1)^2$ and zero elsewhere. What is $\\mathbb{P}(X+Y\\le1)$?","options":["$\\tfrac12$","$\\tfrac16$","$\\tfrac1{16}$","$\\tfrac1{12}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d2432b9eb4f1adb7590ff83a","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Each proposed function is zero outside $(0,1)^2$. Which is a valid joint density?","options":["$\\dfrac1{4\\sqrt{xy}}$","$\\dfrac1{6x^{2/3}y^{1/3}}$","$\\dfrac1{2\\sqrt{xy}}$","$\\dfrac1{3(xy)^{2/3}}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"66fc54ed922827132938e54d","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $U,V$ be independent uniform variables on $(-3,3)$, and independently let $C\\in\\{0,1\\}$ satisfy $\\mathbb{P}(C=1)=\\tfrac25$. Set $X=U$, with $Y=V$ if $C=0$ and $Y=U^2$ if $C=1$. Does $(X,Y)$ have a joint density?","options":["Yes, because both marginal distributions are continuous","Yes, because most probability is spread over a two-dimensional region","No, because dependence always rules out a joint density","No, because the parabola $y=x^2$ has probability $\\tfrac25$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f7bd0d62b202afb93bafe971","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_019","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"The pair $(X,Y)$ has density $4xy$ on $(0,1)^2$ and zero elsewhere. You are given $\\mathbb{P}(Y\\ge X+\\tfrac12)=\\tfrac7{96}$. Using the density's symmetry, find $\\mathbb{P}(|X-Y|<\\tfrac12)$.","options":["$\\tfrac34$","$\\tfrac7{48}$","$\\tfrac{41}{48}$","$\\tfrac{89}{96}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"92fcc936ccca40b992a8298a","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2b_probability_distributions_joint_probability_density_function_3cf1658a_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"On the triangle $x>0$, $y>0$, $x+y<1$ a pair has density $6x$, and zero outside it. Find the probability that $X+Y<\\tfrac23$ and $X>\\tfrac13$ hold together.","options":["$\\tfrac4{27}$","$\\tfrac8{27}$","$\\tfrac19$","$\\tfrac{23}{27}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"275cdf06e98d4210517a6841","time_limit":40}]}}